Z||000003||Bob Englert||01-23-2001||08:58 PM||||Did it overheat with the temp gauge at 160 deg?  The gauge and light are run from different leads on the same sensor.  If the guage is not responding, you might want to replace the sensor.  Easy to do and fairly inexpensive.  <P>I would check the coolant level and probably replace the thermostat as the other have said.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
