Z||000005||sqoach||01-23-2001||09:55 PM||||ok, now that i've had time to cool off a little, i can explain this better. i bought a new stat about a month ago and it's been doing ok since then. i still haven't figured out why it's been running so cold, but it ran fine so i didn't mess with it much. (BTW, the o-ring is off the stat. i took it off because it wasn't fitting down in there very good, and it didn't seem to matter at the time. don't know if this causes a big problem or not.)<BR>it was doing just fine last night. i put about 30 miles on it last night cruising around and it did fine. (keep in mind the temp stays around the 2nd mark (160?))<BR>when it overheated today, i was on my way to the store, after stopping somewhere else. i just happened to look at my temp and it was almost in the red. then it just kept rising all the way up horizontal. that's when the temp light came on and i turned my car off and coasted home. ( downhill all the way from where i was  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) i got home, opened the hood, and the coolant resevoir was full and had overflowed.<BR>and that's the story.||||reg||1
