Z||000023||Raydar||01-25-2001||11:22 PM||||What you're seeng now could probably be considered "normal" for a Fiero.<BR>If you're sitting in traffic, your temp gauge is probably gonna go up to around 220. Then the radiator fan should kick on and drop the temp back to 180-190 or so. When the fan goes off, the temp will climb back to 220, etc., etc. <BR>Try switching on your AC. The cooling fan should come on and stay on, and your car should stay cool. <BR>To fix this wide swing in temp, you can get a 180* thermostat, and a low-temp fan switch.<BR>You can find 'em in a lot of places. <BR>Rodney has exactly what you need, though.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <BR>If it's jumping around really quickly, there may still be a little bit of air in the system. Mine does that once in a while.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
